# XBD 6.4 Character Set Description File
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Whether users can supply a charmap with localedef -f is implementation-
# defined, so a charmap or locale the system refuses is UNRESOLVED, and only
# the behaviour of a locale that was made is judged. creating locales is
# optional (POSIX2_LOCALEDEF): these tests report NOTINUSE when the system
# does not claim it.

assertion  XBD.6.4-charmap-description.001
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.4
class      required
since      1992
says       A charmap with comment lines, empty lines and trailing comments
           is read, and the hexadecimal encodings it gives additional
           characters are the bytes the made locale classifies.
timeout    120
test       t/001-hex-comments-blank.c

assertion  XBD.6.4-charmap-description.002
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.4
class      required
since      1992
says       Hexadecimal (both digit cases), three-digit decimal, three-digit
           octal, two-digit decimal and two-digit octal constants each
           denote the byte they state.
timeout    120
test       t/002-constant-notations.c

assertion  XBD.6.4-charmap-description.003
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.4
class      required
since      1992
says       A range line of symbolic names with an ellipsis defines the names
           in between with consecutive encodings, carrying through the
           numeric part.
timeout    120
test       t/003-range-line.c

assertion  XBD.6.4-charmap-description.004
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.4
class      required
since      1992
says       A coded character value can have two symbolic names, and the
           locale source can use either.
timeout    120
test       t/004-two-names-one-encoding.c

assertion  XBD.6.4-charmap-description.005
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.4
class      required
since      1992
says       A charmap that redefines escape_char and comment_char before its
           mapping lines is read in the new notation.
timeout    120
test       t/005-redefined-escape-comment.c

assertion  XBD.6.4-charmap-description.006
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.4
class      required
since      1992
says       With mb_cur_max 2 and two-byte characters written as concatenated
           constants, MB_CUR_MAX is 2, the two bytes decode as one character
           in sequence, and a charmap without the declaration gives 1.
timeout    120
test       t/006-multibyte.c

assertion  XBD.6.4-charmap-description.007
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.4
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       WIDTH (single names and ranges) and WIDTH_DEFAULT after the
           mapping lines set the column widths wcwidth() reports for
           printable characters; the default without WIDTH_DEFAULT is 1.
note       wcwidth() is an XSI interface in this suite (see XSH.wcwidth);
           that wcwidth() reflects the charmap widths is the reading taken
           from XBD 3.75 and the WIDTH keyword.
timeout    120
test       t/007-width.c

assertion  XBD.6.4-charmap-description.008
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.4
class      required
since      1992
says       A character after the escape character in a symbolic name stands
           for itself: names written with an escaped greater-than sign or
           escaped escape character are usable in the locale source.
timeout    120
test       t/008-escaped-angle-bracket.c
